               <p xml:id="idm183">In 1867 it had been decided to replace the Royal Theatre from 1748 with a new building next to the old one. The founding stone was laid in October 1871, and exactly three years later the theatre was inaugurated, although the inner decorations had to wait until 1883. The building is now called "Gamle Scene" (Old Stage).</p>
